<title>USA: ING Barings to remain in New York - NYT.</title>
<headline>ING Barings to remain in New York - NYT.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>ING Barings, a unit of banking and insurance group ING Groep NV, will remain in Manhattan after threatening to move to Connecticut but will not get tax breaks unless it expands its workforce, the New York Times said on Monday.</p>
<p>Under the agreement, the company has agreed to move more than 800 workers to a building on East 52nd Street and grow its workforce in return for $5 million in tax breaks and other incentives, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>A spokeswoman for the city's Economic Development Corp was quoted as saying in the paper that ING Barings was expected to add 870 new jobs during the 15-year term of the deal.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
